### Orders: the 120 sample orders and the orders OrderPilot stores itself.
### Each row says its source (sample or stored). A stored order has no workflow
### status, only a capture state (draft, submitted or void), which is not the
### order's status. Support and the Product Manager start and change drafts;
### nothing submits an order yet. A sample can be read but never written.
### Sign in first (see auth.http): REST Client keeps the cookies. The writes also
### need the CSRF header: paste the op_csrf cookie's value into @csrf, as auth.http says.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@csrf = paste the op_csrf cookie value here after signing in

### Sign in as Support, who sees amounts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "SUPPORT" }

### Orders, a page at a time, newest first. Amounts are masked by role.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?page=1&pageSize=25

### Sort by orderNo, customerNo, orderDate, shipmentDate, amount or captureState.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?sort=amount&direction=desc
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?sort=shipmentDate&direction=asc

### Search covers the order number, the customer number and the customer's PO number.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?search=SO-00

### One customer, by Navision number.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?customerNo=C-0001

### Capture state applies to stored orders only: a sample has none.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?captureState=draft
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?source=stored

### Order date and amount ranges.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?orderDateFrom=2026-10-01&orderDateTo=2026-10-31
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?amountFrom=1000&amountTo=5000

### Orders waiting on stock. Each says by how much it is short: the list only
### shows the gap, and nothing is ordered for it. The value is `waiting`, never `true`.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?stock=waiting

### One order, with its lines and what falls short of stock.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-0001

### An unknown number answers the 404 envelope.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-20990101-0001

### A bad query answers the 400 envelope with the fields that failed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?pageSize=500&stock=true

### Sign in as WAREHOUSE and the same requests answer amount, unitPrice and
### lineAmount as masked: true, value: null, reason "price". Sorting by amount
### then gives the default order, and an amount range is ignored.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "WAREHOUSE" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-0001

### SYSTEM_ADMIN holds no orders.read: 403, and the refusal is audited.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "SYSTEM_ADMIN" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders

### ---- Writing a draft (P-49, ADR 0047) ----------------------------------------
### Sign back in as Support (and paste the new op_csrf cookie into @csrf).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "SUPPORT" }

### Start a draft: 201, with the number, version 1 and the lines. The price comes
### from the customer's PO, so a role that sees prices must send one on every line.
### A role that cannot see prices cannot start an order, because no line can carry one.
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "customerNo": "C-0001",
  "externalDocumentNo": "PO-HTTP-1",
  "orderDate": "2026-11-10",
  "shipmentDate": null,
  "prepaymentPercent": "30",
  "lines": [{ "itemNo": "I-0001", "quantity": "5", "unitPrice": "12.50" }]
}

### The same customer and PO number again, in any case: 409. The issue on the path
### `existingOrderNo` carries the number of the order that already holds it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "customerNo": "C-0001",
  "externalDocumentNo": "po-http-1",
  "orderDate": "2026-11-10",
  "shipmentDate": null,
  "prepaymentPercent": "30",
  "lines": [{ "itemNo": "I-0001", "quantity": "5", "unitPrice": "12.50" }]
}

### Change a draft. Send the version you read and only the fields that change.
### A stale version, a submitted order and a void order each answer 409.
@orderNo = {{created.response.body.$.data.orderNo}}
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderNo}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "version": 1, "prepaymentPercent": "50" }

### Void a draft, with a reason. The version is now 2. This frees the PO number.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderNo}}/void
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "version": 2, "reason": "Entered twice." }

### A missing price, an empty PO number or no lines: 400, with the issue paths.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "customerNo": "C-0001",
  "externalDocumentNo": "  ",
  "orderDate": "2026-11-10",
  "shipmentDate": null,
  "prepaymentPercent": "0",
  "lines": []
}

### A void without a reason: 400.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderNo}}/void
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "version": 2, "reason": "   " }

### A number that does not exist: 404.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-20990101-0001
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "version": 1, "prepaymentPercent": "50" }

### A sample is not stored: 404.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/SO-0001
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "version": 1, "prepaymentPercent": "50" }

### Warehouse holds neither orders.create nor orders.edit: 403, audited.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "WAREHOUSE" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "customerNo": "C-0001",
  "externalDocumentNo": "PO-HTTP-2",
  "orderDate": "2026-11-10",
  "shipmentDate": null,
  "prepaymentPercent": "0",
  "lines": [{ "itemNo": "I-0001", "quantity": "1" }]
}

### No session: 401. Sign out first (see auth.http), then send the write.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerNo": "C-0001" }
